    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d127">

                <pb facs="0287" n="271" sameAs="frus:frus1950v04/pg271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.004/3–150</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the President to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-03-01">March 1, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I had a conversation with David Sarnoff<anchor n="1" xml:id="d127-f1"/> the other
                    day, regarding the exploitation of the Voice of America.</p>
                <p>He suggested a committee, consisting of himself, Senator McMahon,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d127-f2"/> Senator McFarland<anchor n="3" xml:id="d127-f3"/>—on
                    account of his Chairmanship of the Subcommittee on Communications in the Senate,
                    Under Secretary of Defense Stephen Early, and Assistant Secretary of State
                    Barrett, to look into the problem of improving the Voice of America.</p>
                <p>I wish you would consider that, and we will discuss it when you come over
                        tomorrow.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d127-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H[<hi rendition="#small-caps">arry</hi>] S. T[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ruman</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d127-f1" n="1" xml:id="d127-f1-content">
                <p>Chairman of the Radio Corporation of America.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d127-f2" n="2" xml:id="d127-f2-content">
                <p>Senator Brien McMahon of Connecticut.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d127-f3" n="3" xml:id="d127-f3-content">
                <p>Senator Ernest W. McFarland of Arizona.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d127-f4" n="4" xml:id="d127-f4-content">
                <p>A marginal handwritten notation on the source text indicates that Secretary of
                    State Acheson discussed this memorandum with President Truman on March 2; see
                    also Assistant Secretary Barrett’s memorandum of March 2 to Secretary Acheson,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
